      "writtenOn": "2017-07-25T10:04:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Renamed the method to setNewConnectionPool() and added the comment:\n// A private connection pool just for this Network.\n\nIs that sufficient? I could add a ConnectionPool abstraction that is not OkHttp\u0027s, in order to keep the \"new\" here, but that adds boilerplate.\n\nRe. ResponseCache: No, there are never separate response caches for each Network.\n\na) As far as I can see, there is no ResponseCache at all unless one is configured.\nb) If ResponseCache is configured via ResponseCache.setDefault(ResponseCache), then that singleton cache is used for / shared between all connections, including the ones created by HttpURLConnectionFactory.\n\nThe corresponding logic in HttpHandler.java is:\n\n        ResponseCache responseCache \u003d ResponseCache.getDefault();\n        if (responseCache !\u003d null) {\n            AndroidInternal.setResponseCache(okUrlFactory, responseCache);\n        }\n\n\nAlso see the corresponding comment that used to be in line 282 in this file and is now in HttpURLConnectionFactory.java:\n\n  // TODO: HttpHandler creates OkUrlFactory instances that share the default ResponseCache.\n  // Could this cause unexpected behavior?\n\nDo you think that this behavior is wrong/unexpected? (This question appears orthogonal to this CL since this CL does not intend to change any behavior - it\u0027s only a refactoring).",
